Mythix DualShock 4 native PlayStation mode for GE's xinput (MYTHIX_DS4_GLYPHS=1).

Origin : Luna's xinput DS4 work in Neutron-11.0-21199 (dlls/xinput1_3/main.c,
         2026-10-05), carried onto the GE Sony XInput stack of the 11.19 tree.
         Her full Neutron-line change is kept in patches/mythix-ds4-xinput/.

GE 11.19 ships xzn's Sony stack (proton-ds5-haptic 0197-0204): a DualShock 4 /
DualSense on hidraw is also an XInput controller when PROTON_SONY_AUTO_XINPUT=1
(GE-Proton's default, and the neutron launcher's), and that slot steps aside when
a game reads the pad natively or Steam Input owns it. This patch adds Luna's
switch on top, for games with native PlayStation support (Cyberpunk 2077, RDR2,
Elden Ring, The Witcher 3; the Mythix Launcher sets it for them):

  MYTHIX_DS4_GLYPHS=1  The pad never shows up in XInputGetState(Ex) or
                       XInputGetKeystroke, so the game takes input and
                       PlayStation glyphs from its own HID path. XInput still
                       opens the pad (its own HID collection, as Luna's Sony
                       direct path did), so XInputSetState rumbles it: Cyberpunk
                       2077 drives vibration through XInput. GE's Sony rumble
                       translation sends the native report (USB 0x05 or
                       Bluetooth 0x11). Capabilities report the real Sony IDs,
                       the automatic fallback is off, and dinput keeps the Sony
                       identity.

11.19-3 shipped a first version of this patch that kept the pad out of XInput
entirely. Glyphs were right but rumble was gone, because XInputSetState had no
pad to send to.

Curated 2026-10-07 against the mythix-11.19 tree (GE a3f58c5 + 0001 + 0002).
